  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Groups, studies and people working in this space",
   "text": "The Danon Foundation is a patient group based in the United States that describes itself as a community of people living with or affected by Danon disease [Ebb89110, E5453000]. A group called DanonDisease.org, based in the United States, provides information for patients and families and runs a registry that patients can join to learn more about the condition [E5eaeabc, Ea66a030, E0d1acb7]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Rocket Pharmaceuticals Inc. runs a recruiting Phase 2 gene therapy study of RP-A501 for male patients with Danon disease, with sites in the United States, Germany, Italy, and the United Kingdom [Ee764f20, Ec165b8d, E77e875f, E5e48ead, E1668b79, E4192620]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Rocket Pharmaceuticals Inc. also runs a recruiting Danon Disease Natural History Study with sites in the United States, Germany, Israel, Italy, and Spain [E822f114, Ea370024, E9cadb6d, Efeffc76, E82505d2, Eadecf2e, Edfa898e], and ran a now-completed natural history study with sites in Czechia, France, Ireland, Italy, and Spain [E518cc81, E517d94f, E8c9ce4b, Ef9f78bd, E87eb350, Eae5d3a2, Ec22f80f]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Duke University runs a recruiting natural history study of rare glycogen storage diseases that includes Danon disease, with a site in the United States [E4e42edb, E485f287, E37cc651]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences, Fuwai Hospital runs a recruiting study on precision diagnosis of rare cardiomyopathies, including Danon disease, with a site in China [E948e7e8, E6c048cc, E14467f7]. Heden listed as the lead researcher [Eefb11fc, E042e259, E2e5d60a]. We matched by name a researcher, Ying Sun, to a paper that mentions Danon disease [E6a41567, E0ebc691].",
